;--- this file configures each when to use obrien_recoil, assign a profile, and assign the components.
;--- component descriptions are in the obrien_component_based_recoil_config.ltx
;--- to break down what is assigned where...
; --- obrien_muzzle - flash hider, compensator, muzzle brake, or suppressor
; --- obrien_magazine - magazines
; --- obrien_barrel - barrels
; --- obrien_foregrip - VFG or AFG
; --- YOU CAN ONLY ASSIGN ONE PER SECTION ---

; --- suppressors have to be updated to a baseline to prevent the engines base multipliers from stacking when applied, this is setup toward the end.
; --- each suppressor needs a suppressor profile assigned to inheret the new multipliers, same way as any weapon used, example:
; --- obrien_muzzle = obrien_veteran_suppressor

;--- if you want to assign a new weapon, simply add it to the list like below, and attach the profile/components you want it to use. example:

;--- ![new_gun]
;--- obrien_recoil = true
;--- obrien_recoil_profile = obrien_m4_recoil
;--- obrien_muzzle = obrien_experienced_flashhider
;--- obrien_barrel = obrien_short_barrel
;--- obrien_foregrip = obrien_expert_vfg
;--- obrien_magazine = obrien_veteran_magazine
;--- obrien_stock = obrien_normal_stock

;--- If any weapon is missing one of the sections, the script will treat it as a baseline 1.0, and no changes will be made.
;--- If a weapon has a built in suppressor, like the AS VAL, you can just assign obrien_veteran_suppressor, and it will simply use the suppressor as the base muzzle device.



